From e981e4acc47370f93094211750a859fb08e393cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:42:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: key JIT caches by environment, prune old ones, warm
 a new image's

The caches were kept per checkpoint, but whether a compiled kernel still
applies depends on the environment that built it. Five Llama-70B TP4
launches in the cold-start experiments staged caches from an artifact most
likely prepared with another image and still spent 19-22 s in
torch.distributed init, against 2.7 s with matching caches, and nothing in
the log said why.

- jit_cache.validity_key(): engine and kernel-library versions (package
  metadata, no import), GPU compute capability (nvidia-smi, else libcuda in a
  child process), CPU arch, Python, CUDA toolkit (its version.json), and the
  image tag when the image sets one. It names a namespace such as
  sglang-0.5.20-sm90-aarch64-3f2a9c1b7d4e under <artifact>/servekit-caches/.
- launch stages only its own key's namespace, still to a fixed node-local
  path (/tmp/servekit/caches/<artifact>/<key>, since ninja and Triton record
  absolute paths), and logs the namespaces it skipped with what differs. An
  artifact from before keys is staged as before. With no caches the engine
  still JITs into the node-local copy rather than $HOME. A cache variable
  the environment already sets is left alone.
- prepare keeps its run's caches as this key's namespace: copied after the
  engine has exited, published by rename, without the node-specific GPU P2P
  check or the debris of interrupted writes; then prunes to the newest
  --jit-cache-keep (default 3). A launch never writes the artifact.
- --only-prepare on a prepared artifact without this key's caches runs one
  warmup off the presharded checkpoint (save_sharded_state.py
  --servekit-warm-only) instead of re-sharding.
- The launch report records the key and whether its caches were staged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
